WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.334 --> 00:00:02.535
-Looking good, buddy.
Welcome back to the show.

00:00:02.535 --> 00:00:03.869
Thanks for being here.
-Thanks for having me.

00:00:03.869 --> 00:00:08.574
Before we get into the notes,
I've been on the show

00:00:08.574 --> 00:00:11.176
six, maybe seven times.

00:00:11.176 --> 00:00:14.380
And a little offended.

00:00:14.380 --> 00:00:20.386
We haven't played a game yet,
and I was wondering why

00:00:20.386 --> 00:00:23.522
I'm always talking
and not, like,

00:00:23.522 --> 00:00:27.293
participating in the fun games.

00:00:27.293 --> 00:00:30.262
-Because you
kind of are the fun game.

00:00:30.262 --> 00:00:31.497
-Oh, I am the game.

00:00:31.497 --> 00:00:32.498
-Yeah, we want to...

00:00:32.498 --> 00:00:33.933
[ Cheers and applause ]
-Alright.

00:00:33.933 --> 00:00:36.235
-We want to play -- We're all
playing right now with you.

00:00:36.235 --> 00:00:37.369
You are the game.

00:00:37.369 --> 00:00:39.238
I would love to play.

00:00:39.238 --> 00:00:40.406
I'll pitch you a game
next time you come --

00:00:40.406 --> 00:00:41.708
-Yeah, let's do it.

00:00:41.708 --> 00:00:43.075
My mother's like,
"You playing a game?"

00:00:43.075 --> 00:00:45.078
I go, "No, I'm talking again."

00:00:45.078 --> 00:00:46.312
[ Laughter ]

00:00:46.312 --> 00:00:48.514
-You're, like,
a professional talker.

00:00:48.514 --> 00:00:50.483
-Yeah, yeah. I am.
I like talking.

00:00:50.483 --> 00:00:54.153
But for my mom,
if we could play a game...

00:00:54.153 --> 00:00:55.721
-Without a doubt,
I will play a game.

00:00:55.721 --> 00:00:56.756
Mom, if you're watching,

00:00:56.756 --> 00:00:58.491
I will --
Please, I will do anything.

00:00:58.491 --> 00:01:00.092
I will play a game.
I would love to.

00:01:00.092 --> 00:01:01.227
I'd be honored.
-Well, thank you.

00:01:01.227 --> 00:01:02.962
-I want to --
What is Thanksgiving like?

00:01:02.962 --> 00:01:03.963
Can you walk me through
what it's like

00:01:03.963 --> 00:01:05.064
at the Maniscalco house?

00:01:05.064 --> 00:01:07.633
-Normally, it's at
my mother's --

00:01:07.633 --> 00:01:09.935
my mother-in-law's house
in Florida.

00:01:09.935 --> 00:01:15.641
This year, due to logistics,
at my father's house.

00:01:15.641 --> 00:01:18.043
And --
-Wow. What's that like?

00:01:18.043 --> 00:01:21.814
-Mussels and octopus.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:21.814 --> 00:01:25.918
No turkey, no yams.
-What?!

00:01:25.918 --> 00:01:31.090
-It's braciole,
eggplant, pasta --

00:01:31.090 --> 00:01:32.358
what the Pilgrims ate.

00:01:32.358 --> 00:01:33.526
[ Laughter ]

00:01:36.795 --> 00:01:40.199
-Speaking of your dad,
I congratulated you backstage,

00:01:40.199 --> 00:01:41.533
but I really mean this.

00:01:41.533 --> 00:01:45.604
I know you're shooting a movie
based on your dad's life.

00:01:45.604 --> 00:01:47.640
And you're playing you.
-Yes.

00:01:47.640 --> 00:01:49.875
[ Cheers and applause ]
-Wait -- wait -- wait for this.

00:01:49.875 --> 00:01:52.644
Your dad is being played by
Robert De Niro.

00:01:52.644 --> 00:01:53.913
-Yeah.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:53.913 --> 00:01:55.648
-Now we can clap.

00:01:57.750 --> 00:02:00.253
Buddy.
-Yeah, it's...

00:02:00.253 --> 00:02:03.522
We shot this thing
in Alabama for two months.

00:02:03.522 --> 00:02:05.091
[ Cheers and applause ]
And...

00:02:05.091 --> 00:02:06.326
Alabama's here tonight.

00:02:06.326 --> 00:02:07.593
And --

00:02:07.593 --> 00:02:09.195
-No, they're actually just
a fan of "two months."

00:02:09.195 --> 00:02:11.931
-Oh. Two months.
-They love two months.

00:02:11.931 --> 00:02:16.035
They go, "Oh, yeah, we were
waiting to hear Jimmy say it."

00:02:16.035 --> 00:02:17.369
-Wait. But --
-So, yeah, so --

00:02:17.369 --> 00:02:20.806
-But do you freak out?
I mean, that's your hero, man.

00:02:20.806 --> 00:02:23.142
-It's -- Yeah, here's a guy
I grew up watching --

00:02:23.142 --> 00:02:24.677
"Casino."

00:02:24.677 --> 00:02:26.445
I used to work at
the Four Seasons Hotel.

00:02:26.445 --> 00:02:28.814
I've waited on Robert De Niro.

00:02:28.814 --> 00:02:30.416
-Yeah, I actually have
a picture of you

00:02:30.416 --> 00:02:32.351
working at the Four Seasons.

00:02:32.351 --> 00:02:34.987
-Yeah, that's me.
The Four Seasons.

00:02:34.987 --> 00:02:36.321
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:36.321 --> 00:02:39.726
-And how was -- how was
Robert De Niro when you met him?

00:02:39.726 --> 00:02:40.827
How was he?

00:02:40.827 --> 00:02:42.728
-You know, quiet,
and, you know, he just --

00:02:42.728 --> 00:02:46.032
He was eating a lot of almonds.
We gave, like, free snacks.

00:02:46.032 --> 00:02:47.666
And this guy was
wolfing down almonds

00:02:47.666 --> 00:02:50.469
like they were
going out of style.

00:02:50.469 --> 00:02:53.239
And, subsequently, now,
15 years later,

00:02:53.239 --> 00:02:54.473
he's playing my father.

00:02:54.473 --> 00:02:57.910
So, my father comes to
the set because De Niro

00:02:57.910 --> 00:03:01.281
wanted some help on
how to do highlights.

00:03:01.281 --> 00:03:02.948
My dad's a beautician,
and in the movie,

00:03:02.948 --> 00:03:04.050
there's a salon scene.

00:03:04.050 --> 00:03:05.351
-Yeah.

00:03:05.351 --> 00:03:08.454
-So my dad's showing De Niro
how do to highlights.

00:03:08.454 --> 00:03:12.191
And my dad comes up to me
after he's done.

00:03:12.191 --> 00:03:16.996
He's like, "How much am
I getting paid here?"

00:03:17.563 --> 00:03:18.698
I'm like, "Dad --"

00:03:18.698 --> 00:03:21.768
-Are you kidding?
-No. He wants a salary.

00:03:21.768 --> 00:03:24.037
-"Dad, you're hanging out with
Robert De Niro."

00:03:24.037 --> 00:03:28.708
-No, he's like, "I'm losing
clients back home to do this.

00:03:28.708 --> 00:03:30.342
At least $1,000 a day."

00:03:30.342 --> 00:03:32.578
-Yeah. Exactly. Exactly.

00:03:32.578 --> 00:03:35.548
Dad. Oh, my gosh. Geez.
That is unbelievable.

00:03:35.548 --> 00:03:38.418
You're in the middle of your
Nobody Does This Tour.

00:03:38.418 --> 00:03:39.585
-Yes.

00:03:39.585 --> 00:03:41.854
-Congrats on that.
You're so funny, buddy.

00:03:41.854 --> 00:03:44.157
I've said it before,
but I really mean it.

00:03:44.157 --> 00:03:47.259
And you crush these --
You sell out arenas.

00:03:47.259 --> 00:03:50.162
You sold you Madison Square
Garden December 28th.

00:03:50.162 --> 00:03:51.763
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:51.763 --> 00:03:54.200
You're gonna be at the
Barclays Center December 29th.

00:03:54.200 --> 00:03:55.401
-Yes.

00:03:55.401 --> 00:03:59.572
-What is it like to go out to
all those people?

00:03:59.572 --> 00:04:01.007
I mean...
-You know, it's different.

00:04:01.007 --> 00:04:02.708
You know, I started in
the comedy clubs,

00:04:02.708 --> 00:04:03.876
graduated to theaters.

00:04:03.876 --> 00:04:05.277
I never thought
I'd be doing arenas.

00:04:05.277 --> 00:04:07.913
So, my act is kind of
tailor-made for arenas.

00:04:07.913 --> 00:04:10.049
I'm kind of physical,
a lot of facial expressions,

00:04:10.049 --> 00:04:11.484
what have you.

00:04:11.484 --> 00:04:15.121
And it's nice to go out there
to, you know, 20,000 people.

00:04:15.121 --> 00:04:17.490
It's a different energy,
obviously, than a theater

00:04:17.490 --> 00:04:18.925
or a comedy club.

00:04:18.925 --> 00:04:21.094
I think the comedy club, though,
is the best place to perform.

00:04:21.094 --> 00:04:23.762
It's 150 people,
you know, right on top of you.

00:04:23.762 --> 00:04:26.198
-But I think you do
something that a lot of --

00:04:26.198 --> 00:04:29.002
For those giant arenas,
you do --

00:04:29.002 --> 00:04:30.703
You have these
tiny, little nuances.

00:04:30.703 --> 00:04:32.238
You'll go -- You'll make like
an "eh" or s--

00:04:32.238 --> 00:04:33.606
They hear you.

00:04:33.606 --> 00:04:36.275
They're listening for that "eh,"
and you get a giant laugh.

00:04:36.275 --> 00:04:37.710
-Yeah.

00:04:37.710 --> 00:04:40.580
-If I was doing a big arena,
I would scream the whole time.

00:04:40.580 --> 00:04:42.814
"Oh, my gosh!
My dad -- he goes --"

00:04:42.814 --> 00:04:45.384
And everybody's just yelling.
"Calm it down, buddy."

00:04:45.384 --> 00:04:47.887
-You got a different style of
comedy, which is fine.

00:04:47.887 --> 00:04:49.254
[ Laughter ]

00:04:49.254 --> 00:04:55.295
You know, high energy,
always happy, always smiling,

00:04:55.295 --> 00:04:58.664
and I look like
I'm falling into a coma.

00:04:58.664 --> 00:05:02.868
So that's why people are like,
"eh," and then they laugh.

00:05:02.868 --> 00:05:04.671
-"Eh" is great.
-Yeah.

00:05:04.671 --> 00:05:08.007
-I want to talk about your show,
because how did it come about?

00:05:08.007 --> 00:05:09.942
It's on discovery+,
which I do love.

00:05:09.942 --> 00:05:11.443
But it's called "Well Done."

00:05:11.443 --> 00:05:12.945
-"Well Done."
Yeah, it's a cooking show.

00:05:12.945 --> 00:05:14.246
-Yeah.

00:05:14.246 --> 00:05:16.949
-And over the pandemic --
I got a passion for food --

00:05:16.949 --> 00:05:19.151
I was cooking, like,
breakfast, lunch, and dinner.

00:05:19.151 --> 00:05:20.886
I felt like I was running a
hotel over the pandemic.

00:05:20.886 --> 00:05:21.920
-Yeah, of course.

00:05:21.920 --> 00:05:23.923
-I was really doing
a lot of cooking.

00:05:23.923 --> 00:05:26.825
I was like, "How do I marry the
culinary arts with comedy?"

00:05:26.825 --> 00:05:28.860
So I came up with
a show called "Well Done."

00:05:28.860 --> 00:05:30.929
It's 13 episodes
around things that

00:05:30.929 --> 00:05:32.898
I'm really interested
in the culinary arts --

00:05:32.898 --> 00:05:35.334
sushi, steak, dog food.

00:05:35.334 --> 00:05:38.771
We did an episode on dog food.
Bartending.

00:05:38.771 --> 00:05:41.373
And it's fun.
It's different than stand-up.

00:05:41.373 --> 00:05:42.975
-Like, what is dog food?

00:05:42.975 --> 00:05:44.309
Like, what do you mean?
You, like --

00:05:44.309 --> 00:05:46.679
-You know, I don't have a dog,
and I used to make --

00:05:46.679 --> 00:05:49.248
[ Laughter ]

00:05:49.248 --> 00:05:50.816
Is that odd?

00:05:50.816 --> 00:05:52.184
-Well, I think
it's just interesting --

00:05:52.184 --> 00:05:53.553
You want to get
in the dog-food business?

00:05:53.553 --> 00:05:56.289
-Well, I used to make fun of
people who used to go to

00:05:56.289 --> 00:05:59.291
these "gourmet" dog-food places.

00:05:59.291 --> 00:06:01.994
I'm like, "What are they doing?
It's a dog."

00:06:01.994 --> 00:06:06.932
So, I went to investigate
what's going on at these places

00:06:06.932 --> 00:06:10.436
and I learned that, actually,
it's better food for the dog.

00:06:10.436 --> 00:06:14.106
It's like --
They serve chicken and beef,

00:06:14.106 --> 00:06:16.776
like what we would eat,
but not seasoned.

00:06:16.776 --> 00:06:19.144
-Yeah. That's --
-You interested in this?

00:06:19.144 --> 00:06:22.448
-Yeah.
[ Laughter ]

00:06:22.448 --> 00:06:24.517
I want to take a look at a clip.

00:06:24.517 --> 00:06:26.819
Here's a peek at "Well Done..."
[ Laughter ]

00:06:28.788 --> 00:06:30.723
"Well Done with
Sebastian Maniscalco."

00:06:30.723 --> 00:06:31.924
Take a look at this.

00:06:31.924 --> 00:06:33.058
-Is that a good amount?
-Yeah. Mm-hmm.

00:06:33.058 --> 00:06:34.160
-And we put it
right in the middle?

00:06:34.160 --> 00:06:35.260
-Yes.

00:06:35.260 --> 00:06:37.930
-Three cucumbers
right behind the tuna.

00:06:37.930 --> 00:06:39.232
And sprouts?
-Sprouts.

00:06:39.232 --> 00:06:40.699
-Okay.

00:06:40.699 --> 00:06:42.435
Now we're gonna roll, right?
-Yes.

00:06:42.435 --> 00:06:46.172
-It's like you're very
particular about how it's done.

00:06:46.172 --> 00:06:48.374
This is very similar to
stand-up comedy.

00:06:48.374 --> 00:06:50.876
The joke needs to be told right.

00:06:50.876 --> 00:06:52.445
The timing needs to be there.

00:06:52.445 --> 00:06:54.747
-Yeah, let's see your work.

00:06:54.747 --> 00:06:58.117
-My first roll
looked exactly like Saito's...

00:06:58.117 --> 00:07:00.652
if it had been
run over by a minivan.

00:07:00.652 --> 00:07:02.054
-That's exactly right.

00:07:02.054 --> 00:07:04.523
Sebastian Maniscalco.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:07:04.523 --> 00:07:07.260
New episodes of "Well Done
with Sebastian Maniscalco"

00:07:07.260 --> 00:07:09.695
premiere every Tuesday
on discovery+.

00:07:09.695 --> 00:07:11.697
And check out his
Nobody Does This Tour.

